  "answer": "An AE should not repeat “immediate deletion.” Under NovaLearn’s standard policy, deletion is executed within 90 days after contract termination: the workspace is suspended for 30 days for data extraction, then active databases, vector indexes, and file stores are purged, with completion within 90 days total [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. Data is removed from active user access and TutorChat queries immediately, but physical deletion of records and backups takes up to 90 days [NL-019#NL-019-S05]. During an active subscription, customer data is retained in the workspace, and admin-deleted documents stay in a recycle bin for 30 days before permanent deletion [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. Any faster “immediate” timeline is not standard; it requires a negotiated Enterprise exception documented in a signed DPA and configured by engineering operations, such as an immediate 7-day deletion or custom backup retention [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. Sales guidance also explicitly instructs AEs not to promise immediate deletion and to cite the official policy instead [NL-032#NL-032-S06].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
